    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** providing the clear offensive anchor. Facing a favorable matchup against Castillo, **Yordan Alvarez** carries an elite 85.99 efficiency score, bolstered by his stellar .451 xwOBA and a notable BvP edge over 27 career plate appearances. **Junior Caminero** (72.80) and **Caleb Durbin** (70.78) follow as our strongest high-floor options. While **Caleb Durbin** faces a pitcher with moderate command (4.57 xERA), his stolen base utility remains a critical engine for our Roto standing, outweighing the minor penalty incurred by the pitcher's efficiency in holding runners. \n\nStrategic lineup construction today heavily leans on platoon dynamics and spot selection. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (64.03) benefits immensely from a favorable matchup despite Henderson\u2019s quality, as his role at the top of the order and positive platoon splits drive his value well above the bench floor. Similarly, **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (66.03) is slated for a productive day; his 16% park factor boost and the benefit of facing Bennett\u2019s delivery style make him a mandatory start in the 6-hole. **Pedro Ramirez** (37.39) was the primary consideration for a lineup spot, ultimately falling short of our 40-point efficiency floor due to Henderson\u2019s 3.08 xERA, which significantly suppressed his upside relative to **Chase Meidroth** and **Jacob Gonzalez**, who despite lower absolute scores, occupy more favorable situational roles.\n\nWe remain cautious regarding the risks posed by elite arms. While **Christian Yelich** and **Josh Smith** maintain solid efficiency scores, their matchups against Gausman and Bibee, respectively, require careful monitoring; Gausman\u2019s ability to neutralize hitters remains a primary threat to our daily batting average targets. With **Trea Turner**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, and **Colt Keith** off the board today, our depth is thinner than usual, placing high pressure on **Lars Nootbaar**, **Hector Rodriguez**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Carson Benge**, **Casey Schmitt**, and **Luis Pena** to provide any necessary late-game pinch-hit support if the starters fail to gain traction.",
